Tear a link down once

Link::teardown() on a link already closed ran link_closed() a second time,
so the closed callback fired twice and the teardown reason was overwritten.
The Python reference returns at once for a closed link.


--- a/microReticulum/Link.cpp
+++ b/microReticulum/Link.cpp
@@ -793,6 +793,9 @@
 */
 void Link::teardown() {
 	assert(_object);
+	if (_object->_status == Type::Link::CLOSED) {
+		return;
+	}
 	if (_object->_status != Type::Link::PENDING && _object->_status != Type::Link::CLOSED) {
 		Packet(*this, _object->_link_id).context(Type::Packet::LINKCLOSE).send();
 		had_outbound();
